Z||000000||Kilodyne||03-18-2001||11:23 PM||||Just wanting help figuring out a clutch problem.  I get a lot of clutch chatter when driving a constant speed. When im accelerating or decelerating the clutcht is quiet as a mouse.  Is this normal or should I be looking for something? Any help would be great!||||reg||9
Z||000001||StuGood||03-19-2001||10:55 AM||||Quiet as a mouse?  Y'mean it squeaks all the time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ?<P>For some reason (actually, no reason), I'm thinking it's not the clutch.  I would start by checking the CV joints first.<P>If it <B>is</B> in the clutch, the only thing that makes sense (to me)is poohed-out damper springs in the clutch plate.  Just some suggestions... hope they help. ||||reg||12
